    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d298">

                <pb facs="0520" n="418" sameAs="frus:frus1935v01/pg418"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.114 Guatemala/80: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Guatemala</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Hanna</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1935-05-23T17:00:00-04:00">May 23, 1935—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>17. Your despatch No. 640, May 8, 1935.<anchor n="43" xml:id="d298-f1"/> We are
                    disappointed at the delay in receiving a definite reply from the Guatemalan
                    authorities. Please inform them that French Government has now closed St.
                    Pierre-Miquelon to the smuggling traffic, effective May 15, and that we hope for
                    an early and favorable reply stating that the Government of Guatemala will take
                    prompt steps, in line with those already taken by Canada, Cuba, Great Britain
                    and France, to prevent the further use of its territory as a smuggling base.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
